    {
      "id": "m4.2",
      "title": "Chords in a key",
      "summary": "Build a triad on each note of the scale and number them.",
      "minutes": 10,
      "skillIds": [
        "m.roman"
      ],
      "reviewState": "draft",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Build a triad on each note of a major scale, using only notes of that scale, and you get seven chords. They are numbered with Roman numerals. Capital numerals are major chords and small ones are minor."
        },
        {
          "type": "chords",
          "chords": [
            {
              "root": "C",
              "quality": "major",
              "inversion": 0
            },
            {
              "root": "D",
              "quality": "minor",
              "inversion": 0
            },
            {
              "root": "E",
              "quality": "minor",
              "inversion": 0
            },
            {
              "root": "F",
              "quality": "major",
              "inversion": 0
            },
            {
              "root": "G",
              "quality": "major",
              "inversion": 0
            },
            {
              "root": "A",
              "quality": "minor",
              "inversion": 0
            },
            {
              "root": "B",
              "quality": "diminished",
              "inversion": 0
            }
          ],
          "chordLabels": [
            "I",
            "ii",
            "iii",
            "IV",
            "V",
            "vi",
            "vii°"
          ],
          "text": "The seven chords of C major."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The pattern is the same in every major key: I, IV and V are major; ii, iii and vi are minor; vii is diminished. So if you know a song as I–IV–V, you can play it in any key."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "I is home. V pulls strongly back to I. IV moves away from home more gently."
        },
        {
          "type": "exercise",
          "exercise": {
            "id": "ex38",
            "kind": "choice",
            "prompt": "In any major key, which three chords are major?",
            "options": [
              "I, ii and iii",
              "I, IV and V",
              "ii, iii and vi",
              "IV, V and vi"
            ],
            "answer": 1,
            "explanation": "I, IV and V are the three major chords."
          }
        },
        {
